Begin Exploring Related Columns
Relevant columns and their potential usage  

• bitcoin_transactions.member_id: allows us to link every trade to a customer, which we can then map to a geographical region.  
• bitcoin_members.region: gives the region for each member – our final analysis is performed at this level.  
• bitcoin_transactions.ticker: needed to keep only Bitcoin trades (WHERE ticker = 'BTC').  
• bitcoin_transactions.txn_type: lets us isolate purchases only (WHERE txn_type = 'BUY').  
• bitcoin_transactions.quantity: total number of Bitcoins purchased – used in the denominator when calculating average cost.  
• bitcoin_transactions.txn_date: trade date; we will extract the 4‑digit year for yearly aggregations and use it to match daily prices.  
• bitcoin_prices.market_date: daily price date; used to join to bitcoin_transactions.txn_date on the same day.  
• bitcoin_prices.ticker: again filter to 'BTC' so the price we multiply by quantity is for Bitcoin.  
• bitcoin_prices.price: close price on the trade day; multiplied by quantity to get the USD amount spent.  
Conditions that will be applied throughout  
• bitcoin_transactions.ticker = 'BTC'  
• bitcoin_transactions.txn_type = 'BUY'  
• bitcoin_prices.ticker      = 'BTC'  
• Join condition on date: bitcoin_transactions.txn_date = bitcoin_prices.market_date  

Below are 10 exploratory SQLite queries (LIMIT 20 for safety) that move from simple inspection to the full logic needed for the task.

```sql
-- 1. See which crypto tickers are present in the transaction table
SELECT DISTINCT "ticker"
FROM "bitcoin_transactions"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 2. Check all transaction types that appear
SELECT DISTINCT "txn_type"
FROM "bitcoin_transactions"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 3. Verify the tickers that have price data available
SELECT DISTINCT "ticker"
FROM "bitcoin_prices"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 4. Inspect a sample of transaction dates to understand the format
SELECT DISTINCT "txn_date"
FROM "bitcoin_transactions"
ORDER BY "txn_date"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 5. Inspect a sample of price dates to make sure they line up with txn_date format
SELECT DISTINCT "market_date"
FROM "bitcoin_prices"
ORDER BY "market_date"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 6. Join a few BTC purchase records with member region and the closing price
SELECT bt."txn_id",
       bt."member_id",
       bm."region",
       bt."txn_date",
       bt."quantity",
       bp."price"
FROM "bitcoin_transactions" AS bt
JOIN "bitcoin_members"      AS bm
  ON bt."member_id" = bm."member_id"
JOIN "bitcoin_prices"       AS bp
  ON bt."ticker" = bp."ticker"
 AND bt."txn_date" = bp."market_date"
WHERE bt."ticker" = 'BTC'
  AND bt."txn_type" = 'BUY'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 7. Aggregate yearly quantity and total spend (quantity * price) by region
SELECT bm."region",
       substr(bt."txn_date", -4) AS "year",
       SUM(bt."quantity")                      AS "total_qty",
       SUM(bt."quantity" * bp."price")         AS "total_spent"
FROM "bitcoin_transactions" AS bt
JOIN "bitcoin_members"      AS bm
  ON bt."member_id" = bm."member_id"
JOIN "bitcoin_prices"       AS bp
  ON bt."ticker" = bp."ticker"
 AND bt."txn_date" = bp."market_date"
WHERE bt."ticker"   = 'BTC'
  AND bt."txn_type" = 'BUY'
GROUP BY bm."region", substr(bt."txn_date", -4)
ORDER BY bm."region", "year"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 8. Compute the annual average purchase price (total_spent / total_qty) for each region‑year
WITH yearly AS (
  SELECT bm."region"                      AS region,
         substr(bt."txn_date", -4)        AS year,
         SUM(bt."quantity" * bp."price")  / SUM(bt."quantity") AS avg_price
  FROM   "bitcoin_transactions" AS bt
  JOIN   "bitcoin_members"      AS bm ON bt."member_id" = bm."member_id"
  JOIN   "bitcoin_prices"       AS bp ON bt."ticker" = bp."ticker"
                                   AND bt."txn_date" = bp."market_date"
  WHERE  bt."ticker"   = 'BTC'
    AND  bt."txn_type" = 'BUY'
  GROUP  BY bm."region", substr(bt."txn_date", -4)
)
SELECT *
FROM   yearly
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 9. Remove each region's first year of data (rn = 1) using a window function
WITH yearly AS (
  SELECT bm."region"                      AS region,
         substr(bt."txn_date", -4)        AS year,
         SUM(bt."quantity" * bp."price") / SUM(bt."quantity") AS avg_price
  FROM   "bitcoin_transactions" AS bt
  JOIN   "bitcoin_members"      AS bm ON bt."member_id" = bm."member_id"
  JOIN   "bitcoin_prices"       AS bp ON bt."ticker" = bp."ticker"
                                   AND bt."txn_date" = bp."market_date"
  WHERE  bt."ticker"   = 'BTC'
    AND  bt."txn_type" = 'BUY'
  GROUP  BY bm."region", substr(bt."txn_date", -4)
),
ranked AS (
  SELECT region,
         year,
         avg_price,
         RANK() OVER (PARTITION BY region ORDER BY year) AS rn
  FROM   yearly
)
SELECT *
FROM   ranked
WHERE  rn > 1          -- exclude the first year per region
ORDER  BY region, year
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 10. Rank regions by yearly average cost and calculate YoY % change for each region
WITH yearly AS (
  SELECT bm."region"                      AS region,
         substr(bt."txn_date", -4)        AS year,
         SUM(bt."quantity" * bp."price") / SUM(bt."quantity") AS avg_price
  FROM   "bitcoin_transactions" AS bt
  JOIN   "bitcoin_members"      AS bm ON bt."member_id" = bm."member_id"
  JOIN   "bitcoin_prices"       AS bp ON bt."ticker" = bp."ticker"
                                   AND bt."txn_date" = bp."market_date"
  WHERE  bt."ticker"   = 'BTC'
    AND  bt."txn_type" = 'BUY'
  GROUP  BY bm."region", substr(bt."txn_date", -4)
),
with_rank AS (
  SELECT region,
         year,
         avg_price,
         RANK() OVER (PARTITION BY year ORDER BY avg_price DESC)               AS region_rank,
         LAG(avg_price) OVER (PARTITION BY region ORDER BY year)               AS prev_avg_price
  FROM   yearly
),
cleaned AS (
  SELECT region,
         year,
         avg_price,
         region_rank,
         (avg_price - prev_avg_price) * 100.0 / prev_avg_price AS pct_change
  FROM   with_rank
)
SELECT *
FROM   cleaned
WHERE  prev_avg_price IS NOT NULL         -- this also removes each region’s first year
ORDER  BY year, region_rank
LIMIT 20;
```
